# FakeWiki: playground sync

When adding or changing public `FakeWiki` methods, keep the playground in sync.

- Ensure `playground-schema.generated.ts` includes **all public `FakeWiki` methods** (no cherry-picking); run `npm run generate` from the repository root or from `packages/fakewiki` after changes.
- Ensure any newly added/renamed public method is visible in the playground method list.
- Add or update `playground-overrides.ts` when result rendering or options grouping needs UI hints.
- Each public `FakeWiki` method must include `@category` in its JSDoc (labels used in the playground, `AGENTS.md`, and `llms.txt`). Add a new label only if needed; for ordering of section headers, see `PLAYGROUND_CATEGORY_ORDER` in `scripts/lib/method-categories.ts`.
- Verify the method is callable from `src/prototypes/ApiPlayground` (FakeWiki playground).
- Keep JSDoc `@example` fenced code aligned with the playground’s default parameter values and options shape (`src/prototypes/ApiPlayground/playground-data.ts` and `packages/fakewiki/playground-overrides.ts`), even when the UI string input differs (e.g. comma-separated page names vs. a `string[]` in the example).
